      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "Complete 437-line linked manuscript read. The signed-graph parity criterion is proved by XOR telescoping and path-independent root assignment, with self-loops and multiedges retained. Exact real symmetric diagonal-sign gaugeability is correctly separated from arbitrary basis changes, rational graph residuals and sampling efficiency. The shifted nonnegative matrix exponential argument is sound for finite matrices and beta>=0. Deterministic search is explicitly a protocol exercise; verified contiguous prefixes and UNKNOWN avoid false obstruction claims. Equal-weight cancellation requires carrier closure, opposite sign and equal magnitude, not merely nonnegative total weight. The Fock no-partner argument uses the declared six-mode order and beta=1/4, a single negative weight, finite length-three facts and bounds on each longer sequence; it excludes no time-labelled/regrouped/general sign solution. References and physical interpretation remain scoped and no model benefit is claimed. No source program or retained tests executed.",
