            "before": "The integrated expansion is nevertheless absolutely convergent. A spin\r\nspecies occupying \\(k\\) of the three sites has \\(k(3-k)\\leq2\\) allowed\r\nhops, so each occupation state has at most four outgoing hops across both\r\nspins. There are at most \\(64\\cdot4^n\\) rooted closed \\(n\\)-hop sequences,\r\nand each has magnitude at most \\(\\beta^n/n!\\) because \\(E\\geq0\\).\r\nThus the absolute sum is bounded by \\(64e^{4\\beta}\\). This is a\r\nconvergence bound, not an equal-weight pairing or a sampling-cost result.\r\n\r\n",
